### Corresponding source (GPLv3 section 6)

The Corresponding Source for the exact sing-box version A-Box installs
is the upstream source tree at the matching release tag in
https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box (for the compatibility pin, tag
`v1.14.3`; for an auto-stable install, the tag of the version actually
installed, shown by `install.sh --status`). No source package is bundled
in the `core-binaries` Release.

### Written offer

In accordance with GPLv3 section 6(b), if you received a sing-box
binary through A-Box and cannot obtain the Corresponding Source from
the upstream repository above, you may request it in writing by opening
an issue at https://github.com/alariclin/A-Box/issues stating the
sing-box version you received. The maintainer will provide the
Corresponding Source for that version (a link to the matching upstream
source archive, or a copy of it) at no charge beyond the cost of
distribution. This offer is valid for three years from the date you
received the binary.

